  {
   "Title": {
    "Value": "Windows Client License Service Elevation of Privilege Vulnerability"
   },
   "Notes": [
    {
     "Title": "Description",
     "Type": 2,
     "Ordinal": "0",
     "Value": "<p>Heap-based buffer overflow in Windows Client License Service allows an authorized attacker to elevate privileges locally.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "Title": "FAQ",
     "Type": 4,
     "Ordinal": "10",
     "Value": "<p><strong>What privileges could be gained by an attacker who successfully exploited this vulnerability?</strong></p>\n<p>An attacker who successfully exploited this vulnerability could gain SYSTEM privileges.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "Title": "FAQ",
     "Type": 4,
     "Ordinal": "10",
     "Value": "<p><strong>According to the CVSS metric, the attack complexity is high (AC:H). What does that mean for this vulnerability?</strong></p>\n<p>Successful exploitation of this vulnerability requires an attacker to win a race condition.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "Title": "Windows Client License Service",
     "Type": 7,
